# Working-tree line endings.
#
# Everything text is checked out with LF, regardless of the platform default.
# Two concrete reasons, both of which have bitten this project:
#
#   * Go source: gofmt treats a CRLF file as unformatted. With core.autocrlf=true
#     a Windows checkout writes CRLF, so `gofmt -l` flags every file and the
#     formatting check fails locally while passing in CI (where checkout is LF).
#   * Shell scripts: a CRLF scripts/check.sh fails on Linux runners with
#     "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text; `eol=lf` then applies only to those.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never convert binaries.
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
